<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Unsleeping City walking tour: Chapter 1</name>
<description>Twelve days of Christmas in the Unsleeping City, from SantaCon to the New Year's Eve ball drop.</description>
<Folder><name>Day 1: The ferry to Times Square</name>
<Placemark><name>1. Whitehall Terminal &amp; the Staten Island Ferry</name><description>Sofia's commute. In the first episode she pre-games on the ferry into Manhattan, then picks a fight with three trolls outside Sean's, a dingy Irish bar near this terminal, and sleeps it off in a pile of trash bags. Later she rides the ferry with Jackson, who explains the Order of the Concrete Fist and its prophecy of a chosen one as the boat passes the Statue of Liberty (Eps. 7 and 11).

Visiting: The ferry is free and runs around the clock. The crossing takes about 25 minutes each way and passes close to the Statue of Liberty. At St. George you have to get off and walk round to board the next boat back. Sofia's Staten Island (her house, the bakery, the Monastery of the Midnight Sun) is never located in the show, so the ride itself is the stop.

Scenes: C1E01-S06, C1E01-S07, C1E01-S08, C1E07-S12, C1E11-S14</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0131,40.701,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Wall Street &amp; the New York Stock Exchange</name><description>Robert Moses' home turf. Ricky's spell to find the stolen Key to the City goes blank in a magical dead zone among the Wall Street towers (Ep. 7). In the Showdown at the Stock Exchange the party bursts onto the trading floor, where Moses forges Sinatra's Law and opens the Golden Door. Pete is killed and revived, and Ricky beheads Moses (Eps. 13 and 14). Pete later sneaks into Moses' hedge-fund office nearby (Ep. 15).

Visiting: There are no public visits inside the exchange. The columned front on Broad St is the classic view, with the Fearless Girl statue facing it. Trinity Church, at the head of Wall St, marks one edge of the episode's dead zone.

Scenes: C1E07-S03, C1E13-S20, C1E14-S01, C1E15-S01, C1E15-S04</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0111,40.7068,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. City Hall</name><description>Past a magical security checkpoint staffed by a goblin clerk, Kingston gives his testimony about the attack on Santa and argues with Liz (Ep. 7). Kingston's wedding photo, which Pete notices in his apartment, was taken at City Hall (Ep. 3).

Visiting: City Hall Park is open to everyone. The building itself can only be seen on scheduled tours.

Scenes: C1E07-S10, C1E03-S10</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0059,40.7127,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Tompkins Square Park</name><description>Esther brings holiday gifts to her blind witch mother and grandmother in a frosty grotto here. They search Ricky's heart for darkness, find none, and give Esther a prophecy (Ep. 11). On New Year's Eve Kugrash uses the Rat Crown to break the curse on Esther's family, freeing the three witches, and the park's trees swallow the Maserati (Ep. 15).

Visiting: The walk here from Astor Place runs along St. Marks Place. The park is busiest around its central paths and dog runs.

Scenes: C1E11-S23, C1E15-S11</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9817,40.7265,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Union Square</name><description>After the journey through Nod, Wally's L train delivers the party back to the waking world at 14 St-Union Sq. Pete hugs Kingston, Ricky downs a 1000-hour energy drink, and Sofia finally tells everyone that Dale is dead. Misty suggests pizza on University Place (Ep. 9).

Visiting: The station below is one of the city's busiest hubs (4 5 6, L, N Q R W). The park hosts a greenmarket several days a week.

Scenes: C1E09-S09</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9905,40.7358,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Empire State Building</name><description>The 'pinnacle' at the end of Dale's chosen-one quest. On New Year's Eve Sofia climbs the outside of the building, past the closed observation deck, to the very top of the spire, and chooses herself as the Concrete Fist's chosen one (Ep. 15).

Visiting: The observation decks on the 86th and 102nd floors are ticketed. For a free view of the spire, look up from 5th Ave at 33rd St.

Scenes: C1E15-S03, C1E15-S07</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9857,40.7484,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. New York Public Library (Stephen A. Schwarzman Building)</name><description>A secret door by the stone lions leads to the upside-down halls of the Gramercy Occult Society. The party first assembles on these steps (Ep. 1), brings back the twins sick with peppermint disease (Ep. 3) and holds a tense secret meeting about Pete (Ep. 7). On New Year's Eve the steps are strewn with bodies, a lion is cracked, and the Umbral Engine below has been sabotaged (Ep. 15).

Visiting: Free to enter during opening hours. Don't miss the Rose Main Reading Room on the third floor. The show calls the lions Orlando and Rovias; their real names are Patience and Fortitude.

Scenes: C1E01-S21, C1E03-S03, C1E07-S16, C1E15-S03, C1E15-S10, C1E17-S06</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9817,40.7531,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Grand Central Terminal</name><description>Home of the clock gnomes. Shrunk to matchbox size, the party tumbles through the food court, where Pete lands on an oyster and Kugrash rescues him as a giant eagle (Ep. 11). On New Year's Eve Rowan holds a fae war council at the Whispering Gallery and the clock, then rides a dragon train from a secret yard toward Times Square (Ep. 15).

Visiting: Try the Whispering Gallery outside the Oyster Bar on the lower level: stand in opposite corners of the arches and whisper into the wall. The four-faced clock sits on the information booth in the main concourse.

Scenes: C1E11-S17, C1E15-S02, C1E15-S12</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9772,40.7527,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Times Square &amp; the Theater District</name><description>The story begins and ends here. The party's first fight is against a hive of mutant Santa clones around a giant ice chrysalis (Eps. 1 and 2). A few blocks away, Misty's opening night of 'Midsummer Nights' becomes the Broadway Brawl against Titania (Eps. 11 and 12; the theater is never named). At midnight on New Year's Eve the Golden Door opens over the ball drop. In the battle inside Robert Moses' phylactery storm, Kugrash eats the Bagel of All Things and scatters into the city (Eps. 15 to 17).

Visiting: Come after dark. The theaters are on the side streets between W 44th and W 47th St, and any of them can stand in for Misty's.

Scenes: C1E01-S22, C1E02-S01, C1E01-S19, C1E11-S25, C1E12-S01, C1E15-S14, C1E16-S01, C1E17-S01, C1E17-S03</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9855,40.758,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
