<Folder><name>Day 2: Central Park, Harlem and the L to Nod</name>
<Placemark><name>1. Central Park South</name><description>Misty Moore's glass-walled penthouse overlooks the park from one of these buildings; it's the most-visited place in Chapter 1. Kugrash and Sofia crawl in through a boiler vent (Ep. 1), Titania's cursed mirror breaks Misty's hip (Ep. 5), and Robert Moses offers her a way out of the fae court at her holiday party (Ep. 11). Once Misty is reborn as Rowan Berry, Rowan inherits the place (Ep. 13).

Visiting: The building is fictional and unnamed. Walk in at the 6th Ave gate and follow the paths north to the Mall.

Scenes: C1E01-S20, C1E05-S08, C1E05-S09, C1E11-S03, C1E11-S24, C1E13-S08, C1E17-S12</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9763,40.7656,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Bethesda Terrace &amp; Fountain</name><description>The Angel of the Waters on top of the fountain is Em, who gives Sofia and Kugrash healing water (Ep. 3). When the statue is stolen, the party follows its celestial drag marks down a manhole to rescue her (Eps. 3 and 4). At the Loeb Boathouse next door, Kugrash breaks into a locker for a pair of loafers, which Sofia turns down (Ep. 3).

Visiting: The angel is real: Emma Stebbins' statue, unveiled in 1873. Walk down under the terrace to see the tiled arcade.

Scenes: C1E03-S08, C1E03-S17, C1E05-S01, C1E03-S07</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9708,40.7743,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. The Ramble &amp; Belvedere Castle</name><description>Santa's sleigh crashes in a clearing near Belvedere Castle. Kugrash and Sofia find the reindeer cut loose, peppermint blood and faerie ivy from Nod (Eps. 1 and 2). In the Ramble, a birch-tree arch opens onto the Faerie Glen, where the party crashes the wedding of Don Confetti's daughter with pigeon plus-ones (Eps. 3 and 5).

Visiting: The Ramble's paths twist on purpose, so leave time to get a little lost. Belvedere Castle overlooks Turtle Pond and is free to visit.

Scenes: C1E01-S18, C1E02-S02, C1E03-S16, C1E05-S02</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9689,40.7793,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. The Met: Temple of Dendur</name><description>Robert Moses summons Kingston to the Temple of Dendur, where Kingston once fought a mummy, and threatens his friends. Kingston slaps him, leaving an ash handprint (Ep. 13).

Visiting: Admission is ticketed. The temple stands in its own glass-walled gallery, the Sackler Wing, on the first floor. If you skip the museum, the steps on 5th Ave are a fine stop.

Scenes: C1E13-S18</description><Point><coordinates>-73.963,40.779,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. The Reservoir</name><description>Under the water lies the ancient cistern where the old aqueduct enters the city: the Rat King's lair. He means to marry the stolen angel statue. The party fights him in a flooding chamber, and Kugrash takes his crown (Eps. 3 and 4). In the first episode Kugrash scurries through the subway tunnels under the park, reached by a manhole on one of the transverse roads.

Visiting: A 1.58-mile running track circles the Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis Reservoir. The skyline view south across the water is the one on the postcards.

Scenes: C1E03-S18, C1E04-S01, C1E01-S15</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9621,40.7838,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Harlem: 125th Street</name><description>Kingston's neighborhood. The Brown family's three-story house, St. Owen's Hospital (where Kingston works as a nurse) and Cosmo's corner store are all 'right off 125th Street'. The house becomes the party's headquarters, and the Browns host Pete for Christmas (Ep. 11). In the epilogue Pete works at a second-hand bookstore around the corner (Ep. 17).

Visiting: None of these places is a real address. The Apollo Theater (253 W 125th St) is a few blocks west, on the way to the next train.

Scenes: C1E01-S12, C1E01-S13, C1E01-S14, C1E03-S10, C1E03-S13, C1E11-S19, C1E15-S09, C1E17-S13</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9453,40.8077,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Clinton Hill: the Chantry</name><description>The Gramercy Occult Society's Brooklyn branch is an ivy-covered brownstone with a gargoyle door knocker named Frank. Esther briefs Ricky on the SantaCon clones here (Ep. 1), the party learns that the 'gray baby' is Nod, monarch of the Sixth Borough (Ep. 5), and Don Confetti confesses inside a runic circle (Ep. 13).

Visiting: The Chantry is fictional, but the brownstones and mansions along Clinton Avenue fit the description. Pratt Institute's campus is a few blocks away.

Scenes: C1E01-S10, C1E05-S04, C1E05-S05, C1E13-S04, C1E13-S10</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9665,40.6896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Lorimer St station (L)</name><description>Pete teleports onto the Canarsie-bound platform with the dying Nod, and everyone converges for the Subway Skirmish. Kugrash's rats kill the crooked cop Epona and eat her onyx badge, and Pizza Rat's die summons the L train to Nod. It runs on the wrong side of the track, out of Brooklyn and into the Sixth Borough (Eps. 7 and 8).

Visiting: End the day like the party: board a Canarsie-bound L here. In the waking world it stops at Canarsie-Rockaway Pkwy. Union Pool, mentioned at the table, is across the street.

Scenes: C1E07-S20, C1E08-S01, C1E08-S02</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9503,40.7141,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
