</Folder>
<Folder><name>More places from the chapter</name>
<Placemark><name>Green-Wood Cemetery</name><description>Sofia mourns at Dale Lee's grave, where Jackson tells her Dale was a monk of the Concrete Fist who was meant to be the chosen one (Ep. 11).

Visiting: Free to visit. Enter at the Gothic main gate at 5th Ave and 25th St.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9945,40.6585,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Steinway Street, Astoria</name><description>The dream-insect invasion: Astoria's storefronts are webbed over by gentrifying bugs. Sofia frees La Gran Gata from her 'bodega of wonders' and becomes her chosen (Eps. 5 to 7).

Visiting: The party bursts out of the Steinway St subway entrance. The bodega is fictional.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9208,40.7569,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cobble Hill</name><description>Ricky's introduction: he carries a girl out of a burning railroad-apartment building, secretly casts Create Water, and gives an interview to NY1 (Ep. 1).

Visiting: The building is never named. Cobble Hill Park is a pleasant center for a stroll among the brownstones.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.996,40.6882,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bushwick</name><description>Priya's art show in a condemned loft 'in the heart of Bushwick' goes up in flames. Kugrash, as a tiny King Kong, topples the water tower, and Sofia kills Isabella (Eps. 9 and 10).

Visiting: The loft is fictional. The Bushwick Collective's street murals around Troutman St and St Nicholas Ave match the art-scene mood.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9236,40.706,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Greenpoint waterfront</name><description>Pete's story opens with a checkup at Dr. Lugash's unlicensed clinic in a warehouse by the water. A reflection in a ceiling puddle tells him magic is real (Ep. 1).

Visiting: The warehouse is fictional. WNYC Transmitter Park, at the end of Greenpoint Ave, looks across the river at Midtown.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9607,40.7299,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Williamsburg waterfront</name><description>Kingston walks over from Clinton Hill to meet Willy the golem near Kent Ave. Willy buys him a bagel and Kingston drives out a nest of dybbuks (Ep. 5).

Visiting: Domino Park, on Kent Ave, is the place to see the waterfront.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9683,40.7141,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Queensboro Bridge</name><description>Ricky sprints across the 59th Street Bridge with his ox, Ox, chasing the stolen Key to the City, and #MarchInDecember goes viral (Ep. 7).

Visiting: The bridge has a path for people on foot and bikes, so you can follow Ricky's sprint.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.96,40.759,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Yankee Stadium</name><description>On New Year's Eve the Hall of Heroes appears at the stadium. After a game of catch, Ricky's Questing Blade receives its secret blessing (Ep. 15).

Visiting: Right outside 161 St-Yankee Stadium station.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9265,40.8296,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Forest Hills</name><description>Kugrash's son David lives here. Kugrash, as a dog, spends Christmas with his grandkids (Ep. 11).

Visiting: The house is fictional. Station Square in Forest Hills Gardens is the neighborhood's showpiece.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.8444,40.7203,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder></Document></kml>